---
description: TypeScript conventions — type-only, no any, no non-null
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

# TypeScript

- Use only `type`, never `interface` (including OwnProps / Props).
- Avoid non-null assertion (`!`); prefer narrowing, guards, optional chaining.
- Avoid `any`. If unavoidable, leave a short English comment explaining why.
- Prefer shared utility types from `src/types/` when they exist; do not redefine them locally.
- Prefer `import type` for type-only imports (`verbatimModuleSyntax` is on).
